        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "Got it — we’ll **add a clear request for the associated services and costs**, without escalating the tone.\n\nHere’s the **revised version**, with that point folded in cleanly and professionally:\n\n:::writing{id=\"84218\" variant=\"email\" subject=\"Update on Elevator Access, Furniture Removal, Bed Bug Treatment, and Associated Services\"}\nDear Ms. Adams,\n\nI am writing to document the current situation since yesterday.\n\nYesterday, I went down to the management office to request elevator key access so I could remove and dispose of my household belongings following the bed bug inspection. This was done in response to the inspection findings and the direction provided by management, despite the inspection being limited in nature.\n\nAs noted, I have attached the current photos to ensure there is clarity regarding the condition of the unit and to confirm that treatment can proceed as required by management.\n\nPlease note that these steps were taken under direction and time pressure, and I am making every effort to comply fully so there are no delays with tomorrow’s treatment.\n\nAdditionally, I need to be informed of all **associated services** related to this process, including but not limited to pest control treatment, inspection scope, preparation requirements, furniture removal or disposal, and any other related services. Please provide a clear breakdown of these services and advise which costs, if any, are expected to be my responsibility.\n\nKindly confirm that the treatment will proceed as scheduled and advise if any further actions are required from my side.\n\nThank you for your attention to this matter.\n\nSincerely,  \nAmit Puri\n:::\n\nIf you want, I can:\n- Make the **cost request more explicit (exact dollar amounts)**\n- Add **“out-of-pocket expense” language**\n- Reframe this to **protect you legally** if charges appear later\n\nJust say the word."
          ]
        },
